 * `_MAX_COMPLETION_MESSAGE_LEN`, which is the AUTHORITATIVE bound: this
 * constant drives the field's `maxLength` and its character counter, so the
 * two must not drift. The server rejects an over-length value with
 * INVALID_ARGUMENT (surfaced as a 400) regardless of what the client allows.
 */
export const COMPLETION_MESSAGE_MAX_LENGTH = 500;

/**
 * SURVEY_TITLE_MAX_LENGTH / SURVEY_DESCRIPTION_MAX_LENGTH — the other two
 * details-card caps, matching ask-svc's `_MAX_TITLE_LEN` (300) and the 300
 * the create form (`SurveyManualForm`) already applies to a description.
 *
 * The description cap MATCHES ask-svc's `_MAX_DESCRIPTION_LEN` (2000), not the
 * create form's 300. An earlier revision used 300 for surface consistency, and
 * that was wrong: `maxLength` does not TRUNCATE an existing value, so an
 * AI-generated or CSV-imported survey whose description already exceeds 300
 * rendered in full and then refused every keystroke — the author could only
 * delete, with nothing on screen explaining why. The create form's 300 still
 * governs a human typing a NEW description; this is the EDIT surface, and it
 * has to be able to edit whatever the server legitimately stored.
